From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiron Builder <builder@chiron.local>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] w2: keep normal command traces at debug level

The W2 command manager logs every normal firmware command with printk().
This makes successful SDIO command completions, including the vendor's
expected -4 status during eFuse reads, look like kernel errors and floods
the journal during routine scans.

Keep cmd_dump() at error level for actual command-manager failures.  Restore
the original debug level for the routine CMD_PRINT() trace so it remains
available for debugging without polluting normal boot and scan logs.
---
 aml_drv/aml_cmds.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aml_drv/aml_cmds.c b/aml_drv/aml_cmds.c
index b74f156..1eebc64 100644
--- a/aml_drv/aml_cmds.c
+++ b/aml_drv/aml_cmds.c
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ static void cmd_dump(const struct aml_cmd *cmd)
 
 #define CMD_PRINT(cmd) do { \
     if (cmd->id != ME_TRAFFIC_IND_REQ) { \
-        printk("[%-20.20s %4d] cmd tkn[%d]  flags:%04x  result:%3d  cmd:%4d-%-24s - reqcfm(%4d-%-s)\n", \
+        pr_debug("[%-20.20s %4d] cmd tkn[%d]  flags:%04x  result:%3d  cmd:%4d-%-24s - reqcfm(%4d-%-s)\n", \
                __func__, __LINE__,  \
                cmd->tkn, cmd->flags, cmd->result, cmd->id, cmd->id == MM_OTHER_REQ ? AML_MM_OTHER_CMD2STR(cmd) : AML_ID2STR(cmd->id), \
                cmd->reqid, (((cmd->flags & AML_CMD_FLAG_REQ_CFM) && \
-- 
